# The showcase's rendered-figure cache. It is regenerated from the sources, it is
# several megabytes of intermediate PNGs, and nothing in the output refers to it:
# the figures are copied out of it and the directory is left behind.
site/.figures/

# The showcase's own output is *not* ignored.
#
# It used to be, with the front page's `index.html` tracked at the root and the
# three example pages written beside it in `site/`. So the front page shipped with
# three cards pointing at a directory that was not in the repository: a fresh clone
# served the landing page and 404'd on every example, and nothing in the build
# said so, because the build had run perfectly well -- it just ran somewhere the
# clone could not see. A showcase that links to pages it does not contain is not a
# showcase, so `site/` is committed alongside `index.html` and the two cannot
# disagree.

# Per-layout stylesheets the showcase build writes at the root.
#
# Anchored, because unanchored it matches at every depth and swallowed the
# stylesheets under `site/` -- which the committed pages link to. The site
# published without a stylesheet: every page returned 200 and none of them was
# styled. Nothing is written at the root any more, so this only guards a build
# run from the wrong directory.
/theme-*.css
